                <run bold='true' italic='true'>* The number of lost orders is computed on an interval level. It appears at every row, but counts only once per interval.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' italic='true'>* The duration of the event is computed by interval, although the start and end time of the event are its actual start and end time, no matter the interval. This is why an event appears multiple times, each time with a different duration, but with the same start and end time.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' italic='true'>* A blank in lost orders means that no order was registered in that interval, and that consequently lost orders could not be computed.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run bold='true' italic='true'>* When a city or a zone appears as &quot;unknown&quot;, it means that the event was manually triggered and, as a consequence, has not been assigned to a zone.</run>
