    <dashboard name='Notes'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/ClosuresShrinkagesReport/Notes?rev=' id='Notes' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/ClosuresShrinkagesReport' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style>
        <style-rule element='dash-text'>
          <format attr='vertical-align' id='dash-text_1' value='top' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97616' id='1' type-v2='text' w='98698' x='651' y='1192'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book,serif' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Methodology:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Book,serif' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Lost Orders</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Operations might close, i.e. disable platforms from accepting any orders, some zones or cities sporadically  due to local conditions like rider unavailability etc. We call the orders we might have received (but did not) during these time windows lost orders. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Why we want to impute lost orders</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Our order forecasts are heavily based on previous records of orders. This order forecast is later used by staffing to assign sufficient number of riders for upcoming days to meet the order demand properly. We do not receive any orders when a zone is closed and this artificial decrease in orders would mean that our future forecasts will also be lower. Consequently, there will be fewer than actually required rider assignments resulting in shortage of rider and in turn closing of zones and so the cycle would go on and on. Thus, lost orders, if not imputed, can potentially create a self fulfilling negative feedback loop in our order forecast and delivery management systems. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Imputation</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The following method is applied at a zone level.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>All events (shrinkages or closures) are first collected. If they overlap multiple  30-minute  time intervals, they are divided into separate events and each is attributed to the corresponding 30-minute time interval (considering its start and end time). If several events occur within the same 30-minute interval, these events are merged into one.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>In order to impute the number of orders which are likely to have entered the system while an event was active, the program looks at the number of orders which were created over the last 7 weeks, on the same day of the week and during the same 30-minute time interval in which the event was active.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Using a linear regression, the number of orders which would have been created during the event is computed. These are the lost orders.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              <format attr='margin-bottom' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin-left' value='0' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            <format attr='margin-top' value='8' />
            <format attr='margin-right' value='8' />
            <format attr='margin-bottom' value='8' />
            <format attr='margin-left' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{5C4016B5-5BE0-4208-9969-0602A333C543}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
